ng communication, laboratory notebooks, presentations (proposal, progress), visuals and captions, technical proposals, and teamwork. Students work in teams to assess a problem and propose a physical design solution that attends to a community partner\u2019s need for their senior design project, the communication and research portions of which will be addressed in this course. This course is a pre-req for BEE 4590, which is offered in fall semesters.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": ["Written Communication: Identify, research, negotiate, and compose various texts to further a technical or engineering effort with consideration to context and audience.", "Oral Communication/Presentations: Plan, devise, formulate, design, and report information via professional presentations for various technical and audience needs.", "Visual & Multimodal Communication: Visualize, illustrate, and appropriately caption visuals; discriminate between methodologies for creating visuals other multimodal artifacts to support the technical endeavor; create visuals and multimodal artifacts that are accessible.", "Teamwork: Connect, appraise teammates\u2019 contributions, and collaborate in teams; identify, negotiate, assign roles for completing, draft, and finalize communication pieces.", "Research: Perform, collect, analyze, evaluate, and integrate deep-dive research that includes both secondary (database) and primary (original) research."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "EN", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2024FA, 2023FA, 2022FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption